# SABOTAGE: A4 (ADR-047 §5.1) gate sabotage — the DEPTH/CHAIN RECURSION GUARD stops being
# live: `with_tool_provenance/2` no longer publishes the ambient provenance marker, so
# `resolve_provenance/1` sees no parent and treats a run started from INSIDE a tool
# execution as a fresh top-level run at depth 0. A governed action can then start agent
# runs (each of which can propose further writes) in an unbounded chain simply by not
# passing a `:depth` argument — which is precisely the bypass an explicit-argument-only
# guard misses, and why the guard is ambient. The named red (a tool that tries to start a
# nested agent run is refused :depth_exceeded, WITHOUT passing any depth argument) must
# flip, along with the marker-visibility test; the explicit-opt red stays green, proving
# what was lost is the AMBIENT half specifically.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_write_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a tool that tries to start a nested agent run is refused :depth_exceeded
# MUST_FAIL: the ambient marker is set during a tool execution
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
